# Plan Review

Plan file: given as argument, otherwise the newest `*.md` in `~/.claude/plans/`.

## Review result

!`{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.claude/skills/plan-review/plan-review.sh $ARGUMENTS`

## Your task

The output above is one JSON record from `plannotator annotate --gate --json`, or an error.

1. `"decision": "approved"`: the user approved the plan. If it carries `"feedback"`, treat it as non-blocking guidance for the implementation. Say so in one sentence and wait for the user; do not start implementing on your own.
2. `"decision": "dismissed"`: the user closed the session without a decision. Say so in one sentence and stop.
3. `"decision": "annotated"`: revise the plan according to `"feedback"`, write it back to the same file, and tell the user to run `/plan-review` again.
4. An error (no plan file found, unknown path): report it and stop. Do not guess another file.
